    "created_at": "2026-10-20T14:38:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-20T14:38:10Z",
    "body": "> Does the required attribute change anything in this scenario or as the select element already exists today besides how it gets valid/invalid pseudos and form submission stuff?\n\nI think it would not change anything behavior-wise. However, I have a few questions:\n- In the selectedness-setting algorithm, would we reuse the placeholder-option concept? If so, what if the author doesn't include one? Should a placeholder-option be mandatory even without `required` in this case (`<select multiple size=1>`)?\n- Alternatively, if we use the first enabled option in the selectedness-setting algorithm (similar to a single-select), would that lead to strange behaviors?\n- Is web compatibility relevant here?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
