    "created_at": "2026-10-21T11:39:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-21T11:39:59Z",
    "body": "> In the selectedness-setting algorithm, would we reuse the placeholder-option concept? If so, what if the author doesn't include one? Should a placeholder-option be mandatory even without `required` in this case (`<select multiple size=1>`)?\n\nIn this case, if the author doesn't include a placeholder, I think it would work as it does today.\nThe placeholder could remain optional with `required`, since selecting no options is already an invalid option choice.\n\nI suspect web compatibility wouldn't be an issue in this case. Do we need a use counter to check whether the first option in `<select multiple size=1>` is a placeholder?",
